by rvanlaak at 2025-09-18T14:33:56Z

@frozenbrain nice catch, the PR now covers that case as well. See commit e6009b3653a3168ad4741cf9bb63ec3f290f1c87 for details on the fix.

The issue related to [the following comment](https://github.com/symfony/symfony/blob/9c99c367eae55ea30e888ac2f53cab5589b0b2be/src/Symfony/Component/ObjectMapper/ObjectMapper.php#L107):

```php
// this may be filled later on see storeValue
```

When the property name differs from the constructor argument name, the constructor argument's value did actually not get filled in at a later time. It are the properties that get iterated over later on, which isn't aware of the constructor argument name anymore (as property field had a different name).

